  <!-- WHAT THE TWO PROGRAMS LINK, COMPOSED HERE RATHER THAN SYNCED TWICE.
       Each program is a manifest root of its own and each lists these, so a checkout made
       from either one gets a private copy. A deployment needs both programs at once, and
       two copies of contract-bus in one tree is the drift `wire.hpp` exists to prevent:
       the four things iceoryx2 compares at connect time would be defined twice.

       So this manifest carries one of each, and the builds are pointed at them through the
       cache paths both CMakeLists already expose: HARNESS_DIR, INTERACTOR_DIR, FTXUI_DIR.
       Nothing is copied and nothing is a submodule, which CLAUDE.md blocklists.

       ONE PIN PER DEPENDENCY, AND IT MATCHES WHAT BOTH PROGRAMS PIN. A tree holds one
       revision, so it must be one both programs build against. contract-bus is b3acc3b,
       the revision interactor-cineform and transport-cineform-tui both pin: it adds the
       subscriber buffer depth that progress_bus.hpp sets. cineform-sdk is 6869d78, the
       arm64 build interactor-cineform pins. An older pin here fails the build of the
       program that needs the newer one. -->
  <project name="cineform-sdk" path="thirdparty/cineform-sdk"
           revision="6869d78c350f78117dfd04e7a74348c440876cc7" />
  <project name="libwebm" path="thirdparty/libwebm"
           revision="6184f4484a826724b5293837134ab9492261b941" />
